cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this preprint without describing it as a solution of Erdős Problem #64."
title: "Excess-Degree Bounds for Minimal Counterexamples to the Erdős–Gyárfás Conjecture"
type: software
version: "1.0.0-preprint"
date-released: 2026-08-21
authors:
  - family-names: "Løvseth"
    given-names: "Zackary"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZackaryLoevseth/erdos-64-excess-degree-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/ZackaryLoevseth/erdos-64-excess-degree-bounds"
abstract: >-
  A conditional excess-degree theorem for a hypothetical lexicographically
  minimal counterexample to the Erdős–Gyárfás conjecture, proving
  |A| >= 2b+s+4 with exact density and edge-count consequences. The global
  conjecture remains open; external specialist review and absolute priority
  are not claimed.
keywords:
  - graph theory
  - Erdős–Gyárfás conjecture
  - minimal counterexample
  - degree sequence
  - degeneracy
  - reproducible research
